# dsv41 + core: spill v2 for prompts with pictures. Recipe 0006 keys a prompt with pictures by ids made from each
# picture's content, but those ids are short (31 bits seeded by 8 bytes of the payload's SHA-256), so 0016's tier
# never wrote such a state. Now a point records each picture's span and full SHA-256 (spill manifest version 3,
# 48-byte entries; a text point stays version 2, its key, notes and bytes unchanged), a lookup matches a point only
# when every picture before its cut has the same span, position and digest, and recovery derives the keyed ids from
# the digests again (a raw id altered on disk drops its point). prompt_cache.Media and Request.cache_media beside
# 0006's cache_key (the server hands over the digests it already computed), rank_wire v2 keeps carry the pictures to
# the followers, and /health and /metrics count pictures_kept and pictures_refused on every rank (a follower counts
# its own keeps and refusals; its stats reply carries them).
# Switch: 0006's TF_DS_IMAGE_CACHE=0 turns it off together with the key; otherwise on whenever the spill tier is.
# Without the tier nothing changes.
# Tests: core/prompt_cache_media_test.zig, the store's picture recovery and a forged same-id payload, spill_tier_test's
# picture keeps, restores and per-rank counts on two ranks. On the pair (spill_check pictures): the picture point
# restores from disk on both ranks; exact.py 39/39 identical with the code in (engine 9983b2f, before the rebase onto
# 0008). Builds on recipe 0006, 0016 and 0019.
# By Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo). Apache-2.0.
